<section id="what" class="svc">
  <article class="sv"><span class="n">01</span><h3>Research &amp; strategic analysis</h3><p>I help clients make sense of complex questions at the intersection of finance, sustainability, economic systems and real-world impacts. My work is grounded in sound evidence, careful framing, and close attention to the institutional, regulatory, and market context in which decisions are made.</p><p>The aim is not simply to produce analysis, but to clarify the choices, assumptions, risks, and opportunities that matter for long-term strategy.</p></article>
  <article class="sv"><span class="n">02</span><h3>Sustainable finance &amp; investment insight</h3><p>I provide research and advisory support to organizations seeking to connect investment practice with climate resilience, social and ecological outcomes, and durable value creation.</p><p>This can include work on sustainable and faith-aligned investment approaches, thematic and impact strategies, financial products, and the evolving materiality of environmental and social factors.</p></article>
  <article class="sv"><span class="n">03</span><h3>Thought leadership &amp; convening</h3><p>I help organizations develop research, narratives, and forums that bring complex ideas into productive public and professional conversation.</p><p>This includes reports, white papers, presentations, workshops, executive briefings, and stakeholder convenings for investment, policy, academic, and mission-driven audiences.</p></article>
</section>
<section class="eng-wrap"><div class="wrap eng">
  <div style="display:grid;gap:12px;align-content:start"><span class="lbl">Sample engagements</span><h2>Eight ways in</h2></div>
  <ol>
    <li>Sustainable, values-aligned and impact index and active-investment product ideation, strategy and development</li>
    <li>Research on the drivers of financial performance in non-traditional investment approaches, including sustainable and faith-aligned strategies</li>
    <li>Thematic, impact, and climate-resilience investment strategy</li>
    <li>Market, policy, and regulatory analysis</li>
    <li>Research design, report development, and editorial support</li>
    <li>Stakeholder workshops, investor education, and executive briefings</li>
    <li>Partnership strategy for mission-led financial ventures</li>
    <li>Development of thought-leadership platforms, including reports, presentations, and public-facing narratives</li>
  </ol>
</div></section>

<section class="why"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="lbl">Why the name · two commitments</span>
  <div class="big">Rigor without<br><span>reduc&shy;tionism</span></div>
  <div class="cols">
    <div><h3>Systematic</h3><p>Disciplined research, analytical clarity, intellectual honesty, and attention to evidence. Complex questions deserve more than fashionable language or easy conclusions.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Systems thinking</h3><p>An understanding that financial, social, ecological, and political outcomes are interconnected. The most consequential challenges cannot be understood, or addressed, one variable at a time.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Italian flair</h3><p>Sistematica evokes both method and sensibility: rigor without reductionism; coherence without rigidity; analysis attentive to the wider whole.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

